{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: founding gaps revision 3 at e695c7b6aa034292ff1372ca489485fe1ed93b74, on all 39 artifacts with packages/room/README.md first. The delayed-delete P1 in review 3eb7bc44 is addressed for recorded incarnation attempts. One P2 migration gap remains before this can close b6b51de7.\n\nP2: Recover or track the pre-ledger base-name repository of a pending public founding. Workspaces.createIncarnation/prepareCanonical now only create \u003cbase\u003e-\u003cstep\u003e; incarnationNames, canonicalDue and reconcile discover only names already in repo-create rows. The landed pre-ledger Room at 9d0d0cbd calls ArtifactsAdapter.createRepo before reading/sealing the genesis; createRepo discards the creation answer and permits a previously created base-name repository. A create that applies followed by a failed read/config/seal or lost answer can therefore leave \u003cbase\u003e and its 24-hour write token with no ledger row. Retrying that same founding under revision 3 seals \u003cbase\u003e-1, but never discovers, cleans or reports the old \u003cbase\u003e.\n\nTwo independent controls confirm the exact candidate behavior. (1) Actual Workspaces and SQLite over the candidate's existing fake namespace: precreate canon without a duty, prepare/seal canon-1, restart, reconcile and sweep; canon remains, its creation token remains active, pendingCleanup=0, nextDue=null. (2) Actual Room Worker/Durable Object over the existing fake Artifacts: draft public, place the legacy base repository with its creation token, found the same genesis on a new incarnation, evict the DO and run its alarms; the old repository/token remain and all recorded duties are done. This is a migration regression from revision 2's explicit unheld-base handling, not a hypothetical new unrelated repository and not evidence that any dated deployed room currently has the leak.\n\nKeep the new incarnation isolation. Before sealing a pending public founding, account durably for its original public base identity when no incarnation ledger existed, including an old create whose answer never arrived and may apply later. Safely settle observed legacy credentials/repository or keep unresolved effects visible and watched; a read of absence or a new incarnation's successful seal must not erase that uncertainty. Scope migration to the exact bound public founding and preserve every already-founded canonical repository and import. Add upgrade controls for an existing token-bearing legacy base, an absent base whose old create applies after the new seal, and an already-founded legacy room with ordinary work/publishing credentials that must survive.\n\nArchitecture: The new attempt names are recorded before each create; names are never reused, and destructive effects are limited to abandoned incarnations. The holder must match sealCanonical(name) and owe nothing; late creates remain watched and abandoned cleanup continues after founding. Room metadata canonical_name routes reads, forks, landing, log and sandbox to the sealed incarnation, while founded older rooms continue to use their existing identity name. Actual workerd tests cover delayed delete after eviction and a normal landing, and NOT_FOUND after a lost delete. This is a sound correction to the P1 mechanism; the omitted pre-ledger identity is the remaining boundary.\n\nSecurity: Founding uses the creation token rather than minting another; revocation proof and complete, well-formed inventories remain required on the holder. Missing public/import bindings are still refused before registry reservation. Abandoned duties persist across seal, and the sealed repository's publishing tokens are left alone. Migration must carry the same guarantees to previously attempted public founding. The smoke harness now reports refused/partial/malformed token listings as unknown rather than zero, addressing the prior nonblocking measurement note. No live deploy, namespace change or credential creation/revocation was performed by checker.\n\nSimplification: Encoding incarnation identity in each creation duty and repository name makes late-delete isolation inspectable without relying on provider cancellation or a later response. It also avoids conflating cleanup of an abandoned attempt with the active canonical repository. Preserve that separation when adding the narrowly scoped legacy migration; do not restore same-name recreation.\n\nValidation: Fresh detached checkout, npm ci 374 packages; all workspace type checks passed. Root suite: 1,676 passed and one skipped, including Git 185 Node and Room 88 Node/290 workerd; separate Git Workers 8 and Git log Workers 11 passed. Root baseline contains no checker scratch tests. Spike dry deploy builds at 867.16 KiB/gzip 202.26 KiB, with both existing spike namespace bindings. Both independent migration controls passed assertions confirming the remaining leak. The first attempt to generate the Room diagnostic used the wrong working-directory-relative path, generated no test, and was corrected before the successful actual-DO run. No candidate source was edited; scratch tests were removed and preserved in /tmp/artroom-checker-founding-v3-diagnostics. Logs: /tmp/artroom-checker-founding-v3-{ci,types,tests,git-workers,git-log,dry-spike,diagnostics,room-diagnostic}.log.\n\nEvidence/read coverage: All 39 artifacts reviewed; 11 paths changed from previously reviewed revision 2 a5185fa6 were read, while 28 exact unchanged artifact blobs were credited to that review, including all six historical live records. Byte/mode comparison shows no deletion and 536 unchanged paths against a5185fa6. The 03:23, 03:55, 04:03 and 04:21 live records were reviewed previously; README and deploy notes correctly say those predate incarnation names and revision 3 has not run live. The 32/34 mutation result is builder-reported, not independently reproduced. Exact revision live public/import/cleanup proof remains due on the coordinated deployment after the fixes.\n\nIntegration/full scope: Current main 9bb700b6 contains the approved amendment 4 contract and pi Workers AI changes. Independent merge checks of b377f170 and 9bb700b6 confirm their entire trees preserve both parents' changes, with no novel or overwritten resolution. Revision 3 still rests on the older founding branch: merge the current contract, bounded-memory publisher, deploy cleanup and pi main before release, preserving all later work. This review does not close MCP stage 0's cleanup finding, Room amendment 3's concurrency findings, amendment 4's runtime implementation, full pi runtime fa6d295a, or the outstanding signed proof obligations. Schedule estimates do not reduce any scope.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d95b755857d2992161ea033829b72e68755d4ec3","binding":"assigned","head":"e695c7b6aa034292ff1372ca489485fe1ed93b74","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:19b6451f6b89c3ccf01c6a520cff8133034bf2f1\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:da4346a7b787f9370abb6b6abcaadaf010c6334e\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ada09a51224683855809eb9fe5f78df0d2786213","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}